template.prompt:
Create an engaging Luganda lesson for {class_level} {term} on the topic: {topic}

Milestone: {milestone_name}
Core Skills to Focus On: {core_skills}
Difficulty Level: {difficulty_type}

Lesson Structure:
1. OPENING SCENARIO (2-3 sentences): Present a real-life Ugandan context/situation where this topic is used
2. VOCABULARY & EXPLANATIONS: Introduce 10-15 key words/phrases with English translations
3. GRAMMAR/RULES (if applicable): Explain the grammar rule clearly
4. GUIDED PRACTICE: Provide 3 worked examples showing how to use the content
5. SCENARIO-BASED PRACTICE: Create 4 different real-world scenarios where students must apply the skill
6. CULTURAL NOTES: Include 2-3 important cultural insights related to the topic
7. COMMON MISTAKES: List 2-3 frequent errors students make

Form your response in clear, structured sections. Use both Luganda and English. Make scenarios authentic to Ugandan context.
